  <rdf:Description rdf:about="#item_feinstein1990high">
    <z:itemType>journalArticle</z:itemType>
    <dc:title>High Agreement but Low Kappa: I. The Problems of Two Paradoxes</dc:title>
    <bib:authors><rdf:Seq>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person>
        <foaf:surname>Feinstein</foaf:surname>
        <foaf:givenName>Alvan R.</foaf:givenName>
      </foaf:Person></rdf:li>
      <rdf:li><foaf:Person>
        <foaf:surname>Cicchetti</foaf:surname>
        <foaf:givenName>Domenic V.</foaf:givenName>
      </foaf:Person></rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq></bib:authors>
    <dcterms:abstract>In a fourfold table showing binary agreement of two observers, the observed proportion of agreement, p,, , can be paradoxically altered by the chance-corrected ratio that creates IC as an index of concordance. In one paradox, a high value of p. can be drastically lowered by a substantial imbalance in the table’s marginal totals either vertically or horizontally. In the second pardox, IC will be higher with an asymmetrical rather than symmetrical imbalance in marginal totals, and with imperfect rather than perfect symmetry in the imbalance. An adjustment that substitutes K,,, for K does not repair either problem, and seems to make the second one worse. Kappa Concordance Agreement</dcterms:abstract>
    <z:date>1990</z:date>
    <z:DOI>10.1016/0895-4356(90)90158-L</z:DOI>
    <z:citationKey>feinstein1990high</z:citationKey>
    <z:publicationTitle>Journal of Clinical Epidemiology</z:publicationTitle>
    <z:volume>43</z:volume>
    <z:issue>6</z:issue>
    <z:pages>543–549</z:pages>
    <z:rights>[26]</z:rights>
    <z:callNumber>[26]</z:callNumber>
    <z:extra>BibTeX type: article
Catalogue id: M30
Reading status: to read
Priority: B
Topic: Agreement
Abstract source: PDF title page, extracted automatically (can include trailing front matter)
Linked file: 01_Literature/library/Feinstein_1990_HighAgreementButLowKappa.pdf</z:extra>
    <dc:subject>thesis:cited</dc:subject>
    <dc:subject>status:to read</dc:subject>
    <dc:subject>topic:Agreement</dc:subject>
    <dc:subject>priority:B</dc:subject>
    <dcterms:isReferencedBy>
      <bib:Memo rdf:about="#note_feinstein1990high"><rdf:value>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;references.bib comment&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The kappa paradox: high observed agreement but low kappa when the&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;marginals are unbalanced, i.e. when a code is rare. Checked against&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;PubMed 2348207 on 2026-09-29.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value></bib:Memo>
    </dcterms:isReferencedBy>
    <link:link rdf:resource="#file_feinstein1990high_1"/>
  </rdf:Description>
