    <dc:subject>status:to read</dc:subject>
    <dc:subject>topic:App reviews</dc:subject>
    <dc:subject>priority:A</dc:subject>
    <dcterms:isReferencedBy>
      <bib:Memo rdf:about="#note_sunyaev2015availability"><rdf:value>&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;references.bib comment&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Selected the 300 most frequently rated apps per store (600 in total) and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;used rating count as a download proxy: "For Android apps, rating count&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;and download count are strongly positively correlated (Spearman r=0.89,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;p&amp;lt;0.001)" (Methods). The paper does not describe the download measure or&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;the sample behind the coefficient. Checked against the PDF 2026-10-22.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value></bib:Memo>
    </dcterms:isReferencedBy>
